build.bat - batch file to compile relf.asm into relf.com and concatenate
            RelF system image

conv.c - this tool converts RelF images between big endian and little endian
         formats.
conv.exe
kernel.4 - kernel source. Main changes are: removed BYE, changed ACCEPT code
           due to corrected behaviour of KEY.
kernel.new - compiled kernel
readme - this file
relf.asm - nasm source of RelF engine.
relf.com - ready to use binary.
relf.lst - nasm listing.

I'm trying to pack RelF engin into standard PC bootsector (512 bytes). At
present moment engine code occupies 538 bytes and it does not contain disk i/o
and does not switch to protected mode. I'm going to create at 1st bootsector,
that switches to protected mode and contains code for disk, screen and
keyboard i/o. After that it would be clear if we have enough room for engine
or not. It should worth considering some kind of decompressing technique to
pack more code into bootsector.
